.TH XUR.STD.DATETIME 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.datetime \- date and time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::datetime;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::datetime
provides wall-clock date and time, backed by chrono.
For monotonic timing, see
.BR xur.std.time (7).
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B datetime::now() -> DateTime
Current local time.
.TP
.B datetime::utc_now() -> DateTime
Current UTC time.
.TP
.B datetime::from_timestamp(secs) -> DateTime
DateTime from a Unix timestamp (seconds since epoch, UTC).
.TP
.B datetime::parse(text) -> Result<DateTime, str>
Parse an RFC 3339 or RFC 2822 string.
.TP
.B datetime::parse(text, format) -> Result<DateTime, str>
Parse with a chrono format string (e.g.\&
.BR "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S" ).
.SH DATETIME METHODS
.TP
.B year() -> int
Four-digit year.
.TP
.B month() -> int
Month (1\(en12).
.TP
.B day() -> int
Day of the month (1\(en31).
.TP
.B hour() -> int
Hour (0\(en23).
.TP
.B minute() -> int
Minute (0\(en59).
.TP
.B second() -> int
Second (0\(en59).
.TP
.B weekday() -> str
Day name (e.g. "Monday").
.TP
.B timestamp() -> int
Unix timestamp in seconds.
.TP
.B timestamp_millis() -> int
Unix timestamp in milliseconds.
.TP
.B iso() -> str
RFC 3339 representation.
.TP
.B format(pattern) -> str
Format the datetime using a chrono format string.
.SS Arithmetic
All arithmetic methods accept negative values and return a new DateTime.
.TP
.B add_days(n) -> DateTime
Add (or subtract)
.I n
days.
.TP
.B add_hours(n) -> DateTime
Add
.I n
hours.
.TP
.B add_minutes(n) -> DateTime
Add
.I n
minutes.
.TP
.B add_seconds(n) -> DateTime
Add
.I n
seconds.
.TP
.B add_weeks(n) -> DateTime
Add
.I n
weeks.
.TP
.B add_months(n) -> DateTime
Add
.I n
calendar months.
.TP
.B add_years(n) -> DateTime
Add
.I n
years.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::datetime;
use std::io;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let now = datetime::now();
    io::println("{}", now.format("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"));
    io::println("weekday: {}", now.weekday());
    io::println("timestamp: {}", now.timestamp());

    let epoch = datetime::from_timestamp(0);
    io::println("epoch: {}", epoch.iso());

    Ok(())
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.time (7)
